:: Quest Init [nobr]

/* Quest Trigger/Tracking Set-Up */

/* Quest Naming:
	These Strings will use the Quest_Name, which is usually the Category_Name (In most cases the NPC this quest is mainly from) followed by the Quest_Title. Quests that have a varaible title or a non-unique title will use their ID instead.
	IDs are not used overall since it is easier to know what a quest is by name.
	
	
Unavailable: These quests have NOT had their conditions met and thus won't appear in the gameworld.
	(Note: New quests added in updates should ALWAYS be put here both in Init and Save Conversion, even if it is a quest that can be unlocked right from the start. This is so variables have time to reset for the day and it doesn't interfer with the Opening Scenes.)

InActive: These quests have had their conditions met and can be acquired in the game world, but has not yet been. Single-Event Quests, such as NPC Introductions, will move from this directly to cimpleted. 

Active: These quests are quests the PC have collected that are in their Quest Log.Only quests that have Stages and kept in the Quest Log go here.

Completed: These are quests/events that have been completed. We will use this array when checking conditions for previous quests completed.

Quest Log: Quest Logs are the details of a Quest that belongs in the Quest Log. Such as Name, Objectives, Descirption, State, etc.
We don't check this to see Active Quests since it is easier in the above arrays and not all quests go into the log.

Quest Log Complete: This is information on completed quests. This will be used to see which Multi-Stage Quests the PC has completed and act as a reminder of this info. Single-Stage/Event Quests normally won't go into the Completion Quest Log. Only the larger quests.

Daily Events: This array will hold the string names of Daily Events the PC has done to prevent them from doing them again. For example: NPC School Bullying can only be done once per person per day. This string is reset at the start of each day.*/
	
<<set $InActiveQuests to []>>
<<set $ActiveQuests to []>>
<<set $CompletedQuests to []>>

